        <idAbs>The &lt;b&gt;DNR Hydrography Dataset&lt;/b&gt; is the centralized SDE data storage for master versions of DNR hydrographic spatial features (effective 2012).  It includes the authoritative versions of the following &lt;u&gt;statewide feature classes&lt;/u&gt;: &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;DNR Hydrography - DNR Watersheds - Level 08 - All Catchments (polygons)&lt;/b&gt; https://gis.data.mn.gov/maps/9152888e541347428ce4ca6a718c8fd0/about &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href='dnr_hydrography_all_water_features.html' rel='nofollow ugc'&gt;DNR Hydrography - All Water Features (polygons)&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; DNR Hydrography - Public Waters Basins (polygons)&lt;/b&gt; https://gis.data.mn.gov/maps/8159243e8b024922b3a2ea19b0c899dd/about &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt; DNR Hydrography - Stream Routes with Kittle Numbers and Mile Measures (measured polyline routes)&lt;/b&gt; https://gis.data.mn.gov/datasets/minnesota::stream-routes-with-kittle-numbers-and-mile-measures-1/about &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;DNR Hydrography - Hydrologic Points of Interest (HPOI) (points)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;i&gt; - in development&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The DNR Hydrography Dataset is a collection of the "best available" DNR spatial features representing MN surficial hydrology. These features originate from multiple sources representing a range of scales and accuracies. All feature classes are (will eventually be) topologically related and will function as an integrated set of statewide features. Most DNR hydro-related layers are (will eventually be) derived from this central data storage so that master features may be edited once and then remain synchronized among all derived layers.

&lt;b&gt;NOTE:&lt;/b&gt; The DNR Hydrography dataset replaces the older DNR 24K and DNR 100K data layers, including those derived layers listed below.  &lt;u&gt;Users should discontinue use of these older layers.&lt;/u&gt;
&lt;p&gt;100K: &lt;i&gt; dnr_100k_hydro_area_features, dnr_100k_hydro_stream_centerlines, lake_dnrpy2, wetl_dnrpy2, strm_usgsln2&lt;/i&gt;
24K: &lt;i&gt; dnr_24k_lakes_and_open_water, dnr_24k_rivers_and_streams, dnr_24k_perennial_stream, lake_openwpy3, strm_baseln3, strm_pwiln3&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style='display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px;'&gt;&lt;div style='align-items:center; background-color:#f7f7f7; border-radius:6px; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; padding:8px 12px;'&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Download&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style='background-color:#003865; border-radius:4px; color:#fff; padding:10px;' target='_blank' href='https://operations.gis.data.mn.gov/api/publicdownload/download/899/water_dnr_hydrography.zip' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Download&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</idAbs>
                		
        
        <idPurp>To provide a comprehensive, statewide hydrography layer which serves as the base GIS layer for all DNR business needs, including mapping, analysis, reporting, statuatory responsibilities, etc.   Examples of uses are regional hydrographic modeling/analysis, basemapping, limnological studies, and linkage to Fisheries data.</idPurp>
                		
        
